  "summary": {
    "intent": "Execute Session 5 of the v1-alpha launch plan: WP E (a NativeName type so registry-equivalent package names count as one identity) and WP I (a directory index for relative `workspace:` lookups). Then address lead follow-ups: a review finding on historical tag ownership, the PyPI sibling of that bug, and mutation-testing coverage.",
    "outcome": "Shipped PR #561 (WP E) and PR #563 (WP I) with signed commits, passing gates, and both linked to trail #357. The Cargo and PyPI historical-tag misattribution is fixed by one literal-name comparison. Mutation testing is clean on the fix diff, except one known equivalent `Hash::hash` mutant to note in the PR body. #563 was merged with main, with the bench conflict resolved.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Package-name equivalence differs per ecosystem: PyPI uses PEP 503, Cargo ignores case and `-`/`_`, and every other ecosystem is exact. `NativeName` in callisto-model keeps the spelling and compares on a canonical key.",
        "The plan's claims were partly wrong. No Cargo `foo-bar`/`foo_bar` equivalence code existed, `ReleasePackageId.name` should stay a String because keying it on NativeName would reorder stored rosters, and `release_decision.rs` needed no edit.",
        "Registry equivalence applies to duplicate detection (E100), qualified selectors and `[[package]]` rules. It must NOT apply to historical default-tag ownership, because a default tag `{name}@` carries the literal declared spelling. Cross-ecosystem fallback and bare selectors also stay exact-spelling.",
        "E100 now covers equivalent names. docs/errors.md and docs/specs/workspace.json were updated, and a callisto-cli patch changeset is required. Whether it counts as `**Breaking:**` is the owner's call.",
        "Repo workflow rules: commits must be signed with no session trailer, pushes use an explicit refspec with no force, and `git ls-remote` plus GitHub `verification.reason` confirm the result. `just ci` is required before marking a PR ready.",
        "Gate commands are `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just test`. Mutation testing is `cargo mutants --in-place --in-diff`, and its diff filter must cover all crates but exclude tests and benches.",
        "A pnpm-relative shape was added to the perf fixture and bench. At 800 packages, `status` dropped from 4.9 s to 0.6 s once relative paths resolved through one canonical directory index."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/history.rs",
          "line": 181,
          "finding": "`may_have_held_name_at` is the early-return path that credited a foreign-ecosystem tag to a renamed package. It now compares the declared name to the target literally for every ecosystem."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs",
          "line": 265,
          "end_line": 275,
          "finding": "TagIndex accepts the historical owner reported by history.rs, so wrong ownership propagates here."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs",
          "line": 220,
          "finding": "Aggregation takes a tag's version as the baseline, so a misattributed foreign tag poisons the version baseline."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs",
          "line": 268,
          "finding": "`native_owner` is now keyed on `NativeName`. This is the duplicate-detection fix that produces E100 for equivalent names."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs",
          "line": 405,
          "finding": "`resolve_id` now looks up by `NativeName::new(eco, name)`. This fixes the E102 for `pypi/my-pkg` when the manifest says `My_Pkg`."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-model/src/ecosystem.rs",
          "line": 234,
          "finding": "`normalize_pypi_project_name` stays public. It is used by NativeName, the registry/pypi URL builder and `pypi_dist_belongs_to`."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/pattern.rs",
          "line": 72,
          "finding": "`PackagePattern::matches_native` still matches on the manifest spelling, so `pypi/my-*` does not match `My_Pkg`. This is a known gap that was left out of scope."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "Writing the regression test first exposed both the Cargo and PyPI history bugs before the fix. The test failed pre-fix and passed after.",
